loop references remain OS in CWA, while 18 partially tested references alre=
ady show OK/PB. Continue punch close-out and tracker reconciliation.

Loop Testing Constraints / Improvements

  *   Valve functional testing: Further Rotork DDC configuration informatio=
n obtained, including Modbus RTU communication settings and 2% deadband. Co=
nfirm command/feedback performance through repeat functional testing before=
 closure.
  *   Wi-Fi / Level 7 workstation: Connectivity at Level 1A remains improve=
d; Level 7 requires further attention following the previous workstation in=
terruptions and lost testing time.
  *   Operator access: Further discussion required with Siemens regarding o=
perator permissions and support for DO activation.
  *   SCADA / HMI availability: Continue coordinating Siemens configuration=
 changes and downloads to maintain stable testing windows.
  *   System 82 digital testing: Electrical, Siemens and commissioning team=
s to align functional testing arrangements for Monday 19 October, following=
 successful simulation checks.
  *   Additional resources / night shift: Consortium planning continues for=
 additional loop-testing resources and commencement of night shift by 26 Oc=
tober, subject to final resource and workstation arrangements.


Forward Planning
The immediate priority remains completing outstanding I/O within commenced =
loops, progressing Punch B close-out and addressing discrepancies between f=
ield testing and CWA records.

The CC2/CC3 package integration forecast is being developed, including anti=
cipated package readiness dates, associated additional loop workfronts and =
advance coordination with Siemens, particularly for ADG integration. Target=
 remains to complete the initial forecast by COB Monday 19 October.

Please continue updating the master tracker and CWA with testing progress, =
punches, hold points and outstanding constraints to support the next workin=
g scope.

Br,
Adam

